## Project Architecture

- **Product**: Dextop (`free_dextop`, package `moe.n4tsu.dextop`) — turns an
  Android phone into a flexible desktop workspace: a virtual display driven by
  a Plasma-style shell, multi-display topology, extend/mirror/external modes,
  foldable laptop mode, Android Auto companions, and embedded Debian Linux
  (proot + native Wayland compositor).
- **Shape**: Flutter settings/UI layer on top of a privileged Kotlin service
  layer (`MirrorService` + friends) that owns the real display pipeline. The
  desktop itself is **not** rendered by Flutter — Flutter only drives
  settings. The shell is Kotlin views (`CompositedWindowShell`); Linux app
  windows composite through the C++ Wayland compositor in `android/app/src/main/cpp/`.
- **Platforms**: Android 13+ (`minSdk 33`); privileged access via embedded
  runtime / shell binder / Shizuku / root, probed and adapted at runtime.
- **Primary language**: Dart 3.13+ / Flutter 3.47+ (stable channel); Kotlin and
  C/C++ for the native layers.
- **Build / verify**: `make verify` = `flutter analyze` + `flutter test` +
  `flutter build apk --debug`. Hooks: `make install-hooks` (lefthook pre-commit).

```
lib/                        Flutter UI (settings pages, l10n)
android/app/src/main/kotlin/moe/n4tsu/dextop/
  MirrorService.kt             display pipeline owner (external modes, extend regions)
  DisplayMirrorBackend.kt      mirror strategies: virtual_display / window_manager / surface_control
  DisplayTopologyController.kt hidden IDisplayManager topology via privileged access
  CompositedWindowShell.kt     Plasma-style shell on the desktop display
  ResolutionRepository.kt     logical desktop resolution profiles
  linux/                      embedded Debian container, proot, USB, PTY
android/app/src/main/cpp/     Wayland compositor + GPU scene (Linux windows only)
third_party/                 vendored patches (material_3_expressive etc.) — read third_party/README.md before touching
planning/phases/             MVP sequence of record
```

### Inspiration sources

- Samsung DeX / Android freeform desktop (behavioral reference)
- XREAL SpaceWalker, pocket-xr, DroidDeck, VSpace (XR spatial desktop patterns)
- VITURE Gen1 HID community protocol docs (viture-webxr-extension, XRLinuxDriver)

### Build & Run

```bash
flutter pub get
make verify            # analyze + test + build
flutter run            # on a connected device
make install-hooks     # once per clone: lefthook pre-commit -> make verify
```

