## Safety / Workflow Rails

NEVER do these without explicit user approval:

- Modify `.cursor/rules/` files (except via `/dialectic-of-cognition`)
- Commit or push to git **outside** `/task-3-complete`
- Push without `--push` (commits are local by default in `/task-3-complete`)
- Force-push, rewrite shared history, or push secrets
- Commit signing material, Firebase config, or service-account files (see `.gitignore`)
- Vendor or commit a proprietary SDK blob (Viture/XREAL official SDKs) — Dextop
  is GPL-3.0 FOSS; use the community-documented protocols
- Edit `third_party/` vendored trees without reading `third_party/README.md` first

### Package managers / toolchain

- Flutter stable channel, Dart SDK ^3.13 — do not silently upgrade the
  toolchain mid-task; propose it first.
- Dependencies: add via `flutter pub add`, pin caret ranges; every new named
  dependency needs a `.cursor/rules/<name>.mdc` spoke + README row.
- Never add a dependency where a Kotlin/platform-API path already exists.

### Verification defaults

- Prefer `make verify` after substantive edits
- If verification fails, fix that layer — do not advance
- Kotlin/Gradle-only changes still run `make verify` (analyze + test catch
  cross-layer breaks; document manual/instrumented test paths in the task file)

